    "note": "Per-model list rates in model_prices_usd_per_mtok are the authoritative figures — prefer them over tier_prices_usd_per_mtok, which exists only as a fallback bound when a record carries a tier but no model id. The tier fallback CANNOT distinguish models that share a tier at different prices (Sonnet 5 at introductory $2/$10 vs Sonnet 4.6 at $3/$15 are both MID), so tier-priced figures are a range, not a point. Cache columns are multiples of the model's input rate: read 0.1x, 5-minute write 1.25x, 1-hour write 2x. claude-sonnet-5 carries introductory_until/standard_after because its rate steps up on 2026-09-01; price a record by comparing its started_at to that date. The harness stores raw token counts and computes no dollars at write time; read-time consumers price tokens_directional per-model. Bump version on any rate/column change so historical records stay re-priceable. '<synthetic>' is not a billable model — it is mapped to the cheapest tier so no-model assistant entries stop forcing tokens_directional.complete:false, and it is priced at zero here because it carries no cost meaning."
